F1 Finding 1 — Bear fallback compile-db command missing jobs + all
================================================================================

Plan requirement:
  STM32: generate compile_commands.json -> prefer compiledb make -C <config>,
  otherwise bear -- make -j"$(nproc 2>/dev/null || echo 4)" all -C <config>.

Before (lua/overseer/template/stm32.lua):
  if dev_utils.executable("bear") then
    return task_utils.task("bear -- make -C " .. vim.fn.shellescape(cfg), { ... })
  end

After (lua/overseer/template/stm32.lua):
  compile_db_task now delegates to stm32.generate_compile_commands(project),
  which already emits the correct bear fallback with jobs + all.

================================================================================
F1 Finding 2 — OpenOCD server task ignored project-local overrides
================================================================================

Plan requirement:
  STM32: OpenOCD server -> use project/default config files;
  honor project-local overrides (.nvim/stm32.lua, .stm32-nvim.lua).

Before (lua/overseer/template/stm32.lua):
  local target_cfg = vim.fn.input("Target OpenOCD config ...", "target/stm32f4x.cfg", "file")
  local command = "openocd -f interface/stlink.cfg -f " .. vim.fn.shellescape(target_cfg)

After (lua/overseer/template/stm32.lua):
  openocd_task now calls stm32.start_openocd(project).
  start_openocd resolves interface/target from:
    1. opts passed in
    2. local override file (.nvim/stm32.lua or .stm32-nvim.lua)
    3. project.openocd_interface / project.openocd_target
    4. default interface/stlink.cfg
  Prompting only happens when the resolved target is still nil.

